+# [2026-10-22] G5 nested lookup port compatibility
+
+- **Symptom**: `KeyError: lookup_rpc_port` in single-container P/D configuration.
+- **Root cause**: `motor/config/node_manager.py` indexed only the top-level store field, while the G5 engine configuration carries it under `kv_connector_extra_config`.
+- **Why**: A legacy Motor config assumption was copied to the native-engine connector configuration.
+- **Fix**: Preserve top-level precedence, fall back to nested extra_config then `0`, retain `int`, P/D index offsets and the UCM skip. This follows the frozen G5 report; it is not a full-file byte reproduction of the unprovided onsite fix.
+- **Test interception**: Six parameterized P/D cases cover nested/top-level/default behavior; an additional test retains failure on an invalid explicit port. Existing tests cover UCM and legacy AscendStore. Old code: four failures/two passes; fixed file: all 74 tests pass.
+- **Scenario**: Single-container TP4 P/D with MultiConnector and nested AscendStore lookup port.
+- **Keywords**: MultiConnector, lookup_rpc_port, extra_config, P/D offset, G5.
